WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.300
Cut a small square from the top of a frog blastula.

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.080
A blastula is the early embryo, a hollow ball of cells.

3
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.780
Culture it in salt water, and it becomes skin.

4
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.840
Now pull the same square apart into single cells.

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.220
Keep them apart for a few hours, and they become neural tissue.

6
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:24.960
Why?

7
00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:30.453
The square is ectoderm, the outer layer that can make both skin and nervous system.

8
00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:33.253
Its cells pass a signal to one another.

9
00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:38.653
The candidate that emerged was BMP4, a bone morphogenetic protein.

10
00:00:39.353 --> 00:00:42.733
Spread the cells apart, and BMP receptors keep signaling.

11
00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:47.073
But separation switches on MAPK, which inhibits Smad1.

12
00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:49.033
That is needed for neural fate.

13
00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:52.857
Now give the separated cells BMP4.

14
00:00:53.317 --> 00:00:56.577
They become skin again, and their neural genes stay off.

15
00:00:57.097 --> 00:00:59.137
Put the three results side by side.

16
00:00:59.657 --> 00:01:01.197
The intact square is skin.

17
00:01:01.757 --> 00:01:03.357
The separated cells are neural.

18
00:01:03.857 --> 00:01:06.597
The separated cells with BMP4 are skin.

19
00:01:07.357 --> 00:01:12.877
In this frog tissue, neural is the default fate, and signals between cells actively

20
00:01:12.877 --> 00:01:13.877
suppress it.

21
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:18.450
If BMP makes skin, the organizer should make something that blocks it.

22
00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.470
It makes at least three such proteins.

23
00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:24.870
Gastrulation is the set of cell movements that form the germ layers.

24
00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:30.150
In it, the organizer and the dorsal mesoderm turn inward and spread beneath the

25
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.550
ectoderm. This is called involution.

26
00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:36.150
That tissue secretes Noggin, Chordin and Follistatin.

27
00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:39.593
None of the three needs to enter a cell.

28
00:01:40.173 --> 00:01:42.933
Each acts on BMP in the fluid between cells.

29
00:01:43.533 --> 00:01:48.733
The third, Follistatin, does this differently, but it also works outside the cell.

30
00:01:49.513 --> 00:01:53.373
Noggin and Chordin bind BMP4 and keep it off its receptors.

31
00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:59.293
The ectoderm above, where BMP signaling stays low, becomes the neural plate.

32
00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:03.557
Now predict. Give an intact square Noggin protein.

33
00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:07.697
Noggin catches BMP first, and the square becomes neural.

34
00:02:08.257 --> 00:02:11.237
Jam the BMP receptor, and the result is the same.

35
00:02:11.717 --> 00:02:15.757
Add BMP4 to separated cells, and they return to skin.

36
00:02:16.317 --> 00:02:22.197
Keep one rule. In the frog, ectoderm becomes neural unless BMP signaling tells it

37
00:02:22.197 --> 00:02:22.577
otherwise.
